g part of  that team changed his life now he's a  permanent tire in the USA sevens rugby  national team the Eagles and just last  weekend he played in Vegas for the big  rugby tournament but now the big  question that I think asking myself why  aren't more people playing team sports a  recent Harvard study has shown that  after college there's a very sharp drop  out despite all these benefits three out  of four adults played when they were  younger but only one out of four still  play today  I asked more than a hundred of you and  the statistics are exactly the same we  here at the GSB are not any better than  the nation's average I like to  acknowledge that people find it  challenging and myself included to play  team sports you might say I don't have  the time you might say it's not flexible  enough for me you might wonder am I good  enough to join a team you might say I'm  worried about my health and you might  wonder Hannah where and how can I join a  team think about it you're putting in so  much money and time for your  professional leadership education what  if you could get a good chunk of it just  by joining a team so what can you do as  a future leader what can you do for  yourself as an individual what can you  do for your company or can you do for  your community I've got three  recommendations first  to enter a recreational league team it's  never too late to get back into the game  or you can try something new Silicon  Valley hasn't stopped here there's apps  for that too  so there's apps to find other players  and to organize pickup games but also  traditional methods as your local  community newspaper a visit at the YMCA  or talking to your friends to  word-of-mouth will work second  start a corporate League team in your  company  this will help connect employees and  create a more harmonious work  environment ultimately leading to better  performance and guess what you aren't  shredded very early on third look for  initiatives in your community that